photo-pass/

# Translation overlays being written. Contract J is enforced by the build, so a
# half-finished overlay in HEAD takes the whole deploy down: that happened on
# 2026-09-01 when a concurrent session's commit swept up de/munich.json at 7 of
# 45 trees. A pass now writes <city>.json.partial and renames it as its last
# action, and this line makes it impossible for anyone else to commit the
# in-between state, whatever they type at git add.
data/i18n/*/*.json.partial
# And any scratch file a pass leaves in that directory. The build and
# i18ncheck both treat every *.json under data/i18n/<lang>/ as a translated
# city, so a working file called _bru_part1.json becomes a city named
# _bru_part1 and takes the build down. Seen 2026-09-02 during the Brussels
# pass. Underscore-prefixed names are the convention for "not a city" and
# data/leads/ already uses it.
data/i18n/*/_*.json

# Xcode per-user editor state: window positions and open tabs, not code.
# It changes every time the project is opened, and while it was tracked it made
# `release.py` refuse to archive on a "dirty ios/" that was nothing of the kind
# (2026-09-04). Apple ships the same line in its own .gitignore template.
**/xcuserdata/

